  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (end of Liberal Arts, all of Bachelor of Arts in Marketing, and a truncated Bachelor of Arts in Operations Management and Analysis whose major list stops at 12 of 15 courses); this ledger covers Bachelor of Arts in Marketing, the only program captured in full. Confirm this is the intended program.",
    "Overlap: the catalog states 6 credits from the major (BUS 340 and ECO 204, marked *) may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements (33 + 45 + 48 = 126, which reconciles to 120). The capture does not state which specific Global Campus Foundations courses BUS 340 and ECO 204 replace.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations courses listed are the 'standard' sequence; the catalog says courses may be substituted, but the allowable substitutions are not stated in the capture.",
    "GEN 101 Developing Skills and Strategies for Success (3 credits) is scheduled as the first course and satisfies 3 elective credits. GEN 104 is required as the 2nd course for students transferring fewer than 30 credits and also satisfies 3 elective credits. Both count within the 48-credit elective block, which is otherwise unspecified.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University. The capture does not designate which specific courses must be taken in residence.",
    "Upper-division: a minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major. Course-level upper/lower designations are not explicitly defined in the capture.",
    "Prerequisites noted: the Quantitative Reasoning requirement must be met before BUS 308 and BUS 401. BUS 495 must be taken last. Specific course-to-requirement mapping for Quantitative Reasoning is not stated.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all University coursework is required; no program-specific major GPA requirement is stated for Marketing."
  ],
